#Layer2: Image Processing and Enhancement
# Layer2 apply: classical image processing techniques
# Pipeline: Filtering --- Enhancement --- Edges -- Processed Images --- Useful Images
# It solve: Noise: random unwanted pixel,Low Contrast: Dark Vehicle blends into dark roads, Blur: Vehicle boundaries are not clear, Uneven lighting: Some area are dark or too bright.
# -- Filtering: Modify a pixel using info from nearby pixels. Pixel--Neighbour pixels--Kernel--Convolution--New Pixel Value
# --type Mean Filter: It avg neighbouring pixels-- smooth or reduce small variations and noise. Study: Neighouring/averaging/kernel/smoothing/effect of inc kernel size
# Neighbourhood means group of pixels around the current pixel to calc new Value
# Kernel means small matrix/ window that moves across the image. 
# For Mean filter: Every pixel has equal weight so the new center pixel is all its neighbour avg
# Smoothing: means reducing sudden change/ noise in the image which leads to smooth or blur images
# What ahppen when Kernel Size Change: as kernel size chnage we average a larger neighbourhood
# Small kernel → less smoothing → more details
# Large kernel → more smoothing → more blur 

# Gaussian Filter: a smoothing/blur filter and it give more importance to pixel near the center. Gaussian filter give highest weight to the center and lower to nearby weights
# It is better that mean filter as it produces smoother and more natural-looking blur because nearby pixels influence the center more than distant pixels.
# It is used for edge detection
# Larger Gaussian kernel → stronger smoothing → more blur → more fine details removed.
# Mean filter: every neighboring pixel has equal importance.
# Gaussian filter: nearby pixels have more importance than distant pixels.
# Increasing filter size: increases the neighborhood, causing stronger smoothing and more blur.
# Mean and Gaussian may blur the edge
# Median Filter: Takes the neighbourhood -- sorts the pixel values -- picks the middle value. The median filter removes them while preserving edges better
# Bilateral Filter: Remove noise while preserving edges. Pixels should influence each other based on both distance AND similarity in intensity/color.Pixel near-- more influence/ far-- less influence.Pixel with similar intensity -- more influence/very different pixel -- less influence.
# Sharpening: enhances details -- clearer/sharper image -- center pixel gets large +ve weight while neighbouring pixels get negative.
# | Filter         | Main purpose                  | Basic idea                               |
# | -------------- | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
# | **Mean**       | Smoothing                     | Average neighboring pixels               |
# | **Gaussian**   | Smoothing                     | Weighted average                         |
# | **Median**     | Noise removal                 | Pick middle value                        |
# | **Bilateral**  | Smoothing + edge preservation | Consider distance + intensity similarity |
# | **Sharpening** | Increase details/edges        | Increase intensity differences           |

